---
export const title = 'Range';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  With <code>range</code> the field holds a start and an end date and shows two months in the
  calendar. The calendar closes once the end is picked. Typed ranges join two dates with a dash,
  such as <code>11/3/2026 - 11/9/2026</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 320px;'>
    <wc-date-field label='Trip' range value='2026-11-03/2026-11-09'></wc-date-field>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>The value is two ISO dates joined by a slash: <code>2026-11-03/2026-11-09</code>.</p>
